Topic 1: File Modes in Python
What is a File Mode?
When you open a file, Python asks:
"What do you want to do with this file?"
That's what file modes specify.
<br><br>
Real-Life Analogy
Imagine a notebook 📖.
Depending on your purpose:
<ul><li>Sometimes you only want to read it.</li><li>Sometimes you want to rewrite everything.</li><li>Sometimes you want to add new notes.</li></ul>File modes tell Python your intention.
